🚀 TCS Interview Experience – AWS Cloud Solution Architect (4 Years Experience)

One of my students recently appeared for an AWS Cloud Solution Architect interview at TCS (4 years experience level).
The discussion was highly focused on real-world AWS architecture, scalability, security, and troubleshooting scenarios.

Below are some of the key questions asked during the interview 👇

🔹 Interview Questions

1️⃣ How do you design a highly available and fault-tolerant architecture in AWS?
2️⃣ Difference between ALB, NLB, and Classic Load Balancer — real use cases
3️⃣ How do you plan multi-AZ and multi-region architectures?
4️⃣ Production EC2 is not reachable — how would you troubleshoot it?
5️⃣ How do you secure a VPC architecture using Security Groups, NACLs, and IAM?
6️⃣ IAM roles vs IAM users — which one do you prefer and why?
7️⃣ How do you optimize AWS cost for a high-traffic application?
8️⃣ Explain Auto Scaling with CloudWatch alarms
9️⃣ How do you design Disaster Recovery in AWS? (RTO & RPO)
🔟 Difference between S3 storage classes
1️⃣1️⃣ How do you manage secrets and credentials securely in AWS?
1️⃣2️⃣ VPC Peering vs Transit Gateway — when to use what?
1️⃣3️⃣ How do you expose a private application securely to the internet?
1️⃣4️⃣ Which AWS services do you use for monitoring, logging, and alerting?
1️⃣5️⃣ How do you approach on-prem to AWS migration?

💡 Key Takeaway:
TCS interviews emphasize architecture mindset, AWS best practices, and scenario-based problem solving over theoretical questions.

